<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 July, from 982 to 1923.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sicily" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sicily.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/982">982 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,044 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kalbid army defeats Emperor Otto II at Stilo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The forces of the Kalbid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> routed Otto II's army near Stilo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, though the emir himself was killed. Otto barely escaped by swimming to a ship, and his plans to conquer southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> collapsed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1174">1174 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">852 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William the Lion of Scotland is captured at Alnwick</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English knights surprised King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-lion">William I of Scotland</a> in fog outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alnwick">Alnwick</a> and took him prisoner. To win his release he accepted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-falaise">Treaty of Falaise</a>, submitting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> to Henry II's overlordship.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1249">1249 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">777 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander III is crowned king of Scots</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alexander III, king since 6 July, was crowned king of Scots. In his reign, later remembered as a golden age, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> gained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Western Isles</a> and the Isle of Man from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-perth">Treaty of Perth</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-iii-of-scotland">Alexander III of Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1260">1260 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">766 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samogitians rout the Teutonic and Livonian knights at Durbe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Durbe, in present-day western Latvia, Samogitian forces routed the combined army of the Livonian Order and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>; about 150 knights died, including the Livonian master Burchard von Hornhausen. The defeat set off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-durbe">Battle of Durbe</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitians">Samogitians</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-crusade">Livonian Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1787">1787 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress passes the Northwest Ordinance</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Confederation Congress set out how lands north-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio-river">Ohio River</a> would be governed and admitted as new states. It also banned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> there, shaping the pattern of American westward expansion.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1837">1837 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">189 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria moves into Buckingham Palace</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three weeks after her accession, 18-year-old Victoria became the first monarch to live at Buckingham Palace. It has been the sovereign's principal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> residence ever since.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1878">1878 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">148 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Berlin redraws the map of the Balkans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> recognised the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, Montenegro and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> and cut back the large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Its compromises left grievances that fed later Balkan wars.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1923">1923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Hollywoodland sign is dedicated in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A giant sign reading 'Hollywoodland' was unveiled in the hills above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> to advertise a housing development. Shortened to 'Hollywood' in 1949, it became a global symbol of the film industry.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 July <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand III, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1608–1657</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/souphanouvong"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Souphanouvong</span><span class="tp">1909–1995</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
